/// newspeak-spec.pdf 3.6: "It is a compile-time error to define a method or
/// closure that has a parameter and a local with the same name." An
/// activation's parameter slots and local slots are one set of slots -- 3.6
/// gives it "zero or more parameter slots, one for each formal parameter"
/// and "zero or more local slots, one for each slot declaration in the body"
/// -- so shadow: defines value twice, and the program is not to be
/// compiled at all: the resolver refuses it before anything runs
/// (`Resolver::check_activation_names`), which two parameters or two locals
/// of one name are too.
class Spec36ParameterAndLocalClash = Object new () (
    shadow: value = ( | value | value:: 5. ^value )
    public main: platform args: arguments = (
        | t = platform transcript. |
        t show: (self shadow: 1) printString; newLine.
    )
) : ()
